@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Support";
}

<div class="mb-3">
    <h1> Support</h1>
</div>

<div class="text-center mb-5">
    <h4 class="display-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h4>
    <p class="lead mx-auto" style="max-width: 750px;">
        IT Anywhere understands why your critical business services are so important to your daily
        operations. We've identified several frequently asked questions and answered them to help
        align our services and technology to better support your business initiatives.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="accordion mx-auto" id="faqAccordion" style="max-width: 800px;">

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">
                What is the difference between fully managed and proactive managed?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Fully managed covers the complete upkeep of your IT environment &mdash; monitoring,
                maintenance, help desk and support &mdash; for a fixed monthly price. Proactive
                managed focuses specifically on preventing issues before they happen through
                continuous monitoring and preventative maintenance.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">
                How is Managed Encryption different from Managed Password?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Managed Encryption protects your data by rendering it unreadable to unauthorised
                users, both at rest and in transit. Managed Password focuses on securely storing,
                generating and managing passwords across your business to prevent credential-based
                attacks.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">
                What is a firewall and why is it used?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                A firewall monitors and controls incoming and outgoing network traffic based on
                security rules, acting as a barrier between your trusted internal network and
                untrusted external networks like the internet.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">
                What steps will be taken to secure my network?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                We combine managed firewalls, antivirus, encryption, regular audits, and staff
                security awareness training to build layered protection across your entire network.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">
                What is Cyber Crime and Cyber Security?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Cyber crime refers to criminal activity carried out using computers or networks,
                such as fraud, data theft or ransomware. Cyber security is the practice of
                protecting systems, networks and data from these kinds of attacks.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq6">
                What makes a good backup and disaster recovery service?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                A good BDR service combines regular automated backups, secure off-site storage,
                fast recovery times, and testing to confirm backups actually restore correctly when
                needed &mdash; especially important for ransomware recovery.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq7">
                Is it necessary to manage our Microsoft 365 data?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes &mdash; Microsoft 365 doesn't automatically guarantee long-term data recovery.
                Managed backups ensure your Exchange, OneDrive and SharePoint data can be restored
                if it's accidentally deleted, corrupted, or affected by an attack.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq8">
                What does it mean to audit a network?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                A network audit is a comprehensive review of your network's architecture, devices,
                and performance, producing a report that highlights risks, inefficiencies, and
                opportunities for improvement.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq9">
                Why should our staff be aware of security?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Staff are often the first line of defence against phishing and social engineering
                attacks. Security Awareness Training helps employees recognise and avoid threats
                before they become costly incidents.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq10">
                What is NetPath and how does it help my business?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq10" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                NetPath monitors the connection between multiple business locations, helping you
                understand network performance and identify issues beyond your own firewall.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq11">
                How does the unlimited onsite support work?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq11" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Unlimited onsite support means there's no cap on the number of onsite visits
                included in your fixed monthly price when remote support isn't sufficient to
                resolve an issue.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq12">
                What is the difference between a network audit and a security audit?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq12" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                A network audit reviews overall architecture and performance, while a security
                audit specifically assesses vulnerabilities, compliance, and risk exposure across
                your systems.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>

<!-- Ask a Question -->
<div class="text-center mt-5 mb-3">
    <h4>Ask a Question</h4>
    <p class="text-muted">
        We endeavour to answer all our clients' questions. If you have a question we haven't
        covered above, send us a message and we'll get back to you.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="auth-card mx-auto" style="max-width: 600px;"> 
    <form>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label">Your Name</label>
            <input class="form-control" placeholder="Full name" />
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label">Your Email</label>
            <input type="email" class="form-control" placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label">Your Question</label>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="4" placeholder="Type your question here..."></textarea>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary w-100" disabled>Send Message</button>
    </form>
</div>